  {
   "id": "jkzoaGqJEgAJ",
   "from": "Joshua Spiewak",
   "author": "299a5089d6c6c523",
   "date": "2016-07-28T21:04:49Z",
   "subject": "Re: [shinyapps-users] Does shinyapps.io support bedtools? Is there a way to install external linux tools?",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">For public packages, it is possible to create an script to install additional system dependencies. See the <a href=\"https://github.com/rstudio/shinyapps-package-dependencies\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://github.com/rstudio/shinyapps-package-dependencies&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792361765874000&amp;usg=AOvVaw2s2L8lHRp1KkS7HbAcccFJ\">shinyapps-package-dependencies</a> repo.<div><br></div><div>For private packages, there is no mechanism for installing system dependencies.</div><div><br></div><div>As far as calling scripts, you are welcome to include scripts in your bundle and call them from your Shiny app.</div><div><br></div><div>For bedtools, there is a bedr pacakge, so you could open a pull request (fasted path, alternatively you could open an issue and we will slot the work into our schedule) in the <a href=\"https://github.com/rstudio/shinyapps-package-dependencies\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://github.com/rstudio/shinyapps-package-dependencies&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792361765874000&amp;usg=AOvVaw2s2L8lHRp1KkS7HbAcccFJ\">shinyapps-package-dependencies</a> repo for that package which installs bedtools, declare the library in your code, and then call it via the package or your scripts.</div></div>"
    ],
